spans.s:
māghá, a. (ī) relating to the asterism 🞄Maghā;
 m. N. of a month (January-February);
 🞄N. of the author of the Śisupālavadha 🞄(composed before the end of the tenth century): 🞄-kāvya, n. Māghaʼs poem, the Śiśupālavadha.

maghá-van, a. (V.;
 strg. st. -vān;
 🞄mid. -vat;
 wk. maghon = magha‿un: nm. -vā 🞄or -vān;
 f. maghónī) bountiful, munificent;
 🞄m. bestower of gifts, esp. of institutors 🞄of sacrifices, who pay the priests and singers;
 🞄the Bounteous One (Indra);
 in C. only ep. 🞄of Indra.
